+Tailored Operator Runbook — Convert Aegis from scaffold → validated production (template)
+
+Purpose
+- A step‑by‑step runbook for an operator to convert Aegis from scaffold to validated production for a representative vehicle or robot class. Copy this file and edit fields marked <...>.
+
+Prerequisites
+- Representative hardware provisioned:
+  - Controller/ECU hosts (hostnames/IPs). Example: ecu-1, ecu-2
+  - Network: CAN/CAN-FD interfaces, TSN switches (if used)
+  - HIL rig accessible via operator network
+  - Self-hosted runners labeled and hardened per ops/hw/ci/runner_provision/ansible_provision_sample.yml
+- Secrets configured in CI / local env:
+  - COSIGN_KMS_URI (KMS URI of cosign key)
+  - REKOR_SERVER (rekor server URL)
+  - WATTTIME_API_KEY (WattTime key for carbon)
+  - S3_UPLOAD (evidence bucket path)
+  - MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI
+
+Top-level sequence (one run)
+1) Preflight checks
+   - Confirm runners: local and builder runners are labeled (gpu, inferentia, graphcore, habana).
+   - Confirm tools present on at least one runner: cosign, rekor-cli, apalache-mc, neuron-cc, poprun, habana_info, cansend/candump, tsntool, onnxruntime.
+   - Place golden traces: /opt/aegis/golden_trace.ndjson
+   - Create target list: ops/av/rt/rt_sweep_targets.json (format: [{"host":"ecu-1","iface":"can0"}, ...])
+
+2) Hardware RT proof (per-target)
+   - Run a single-target validation:
+     NODE=ecu-1 OUT=/tmp/aegis_rt_ecu1 S3_UPLOAD=<S3_UPLOAD> COSIGN_KMS_URI=<COSIGN_KMS_URI> \
+       ./ops/av/rt/vehicle_rt_validation.sh --out /tmp/aegis_rt_ecu1
+   - Or run sweep across targets:
+     TARGETS="ecu-1:can0,ecu-2:eth1" COSIGN_KMS_URI=<COSIGN_KMS_URI> S3_UPLOAD=<S3_UPLOAD> \
+       ./ops/av/rt/run_hw_rt_sweep.sh /tmp/rt_sweep
+   - Inspect proof:
+     - /tmp/.../rt_slo_proof.json — check p99_ok == true and safe_ok == true
+     - If failures: triage IRQ, CPU isolation, PREEMPT_RT kernel settings, CPU affinity, NIC driver parameters.
+
+3) Controller HIL Campaigns & Formal
+   - Define test matrix CSV: ops/av/test_matrices/detailed_test_matrix.csv (populate any missing scenarios).
+   - Run campaign:
+     python3 ops/robotics/control/certified/hil_campaign_manager.py --scenarios "run_brake_test.sh" "run_steer_test.sh" --golden /opt/aegis/golden_trace.ndjson --out /tmp/hil_campaign
+   - Review GH issues opened by campaign manager for triage.
+   - Run Apalache triage:
+     ./ops/formal/apalache_triage_runner.sh /tmp/hil_campaign
+   - Iterate on controller code and TLA+ specs until HIL scenarios pass and Apalache counterexamples resolved.
+
+4) Perception long-tail & OOD
+   - Generate scenario packs:
+     python3 ops/av/sim_hil/carla_scenario_pack_generator.py --count 200 --out /tmp/scenario_pack.tar.gz
+   - Run simulation cluster (Argo):
+     python3 ops/av/perception/scale/run_simulation_cluster.py --packs 10 --scenarios-per-pack 100 --parallel 4 --out /tmp/sim_cluster_run
+   - Collect failures and create adversarial dataset:
+     python3 ops/av/perception/scale/ood_failure_collector.py --failures /tmp/sim_cluster_run/failures.json --out /tmp/adv_dataset --trigger
+   - Retrain/harden and export ONNX; run ops/hw/validation/npu_readiness_check.py on labeled NPU runners.
+
+5) Supply‑chain enforcement (CI)
+   - Harden builder runners and enable CI:
+     - Ensure cosign + rekor-cli installed and that builder images sign artifacts with COSIGN_KMS_URI.
+     - Activate workflow: .github/workflows/enforce_provenance_carbon.yml
+   - Test: run strict_provenance_enforcer.py locally against manifests and verify it fails on unsigned images.
+
+6) Carbon gate tuning
+   - Monitor for two weeks:
+     python3 ops/carbon/carbon_gate_tuner.py --mode monitor --out /tmp/carbon_monitor.log
+   - Tune Aegis_CARBON_PROMOTE_THRESHOLD_GCO2 and window size until acceptable.
+   - Enable enforce mode in CI with override artifacts signed via ops/carbon/override_signer.py created by Platform Owner.
+
+7) Produce safety case & submit
+   - Build safety case:
+     python3 ops/av/ops/safety_case_builder.py --base . --out /tmp/safety_case_bundle.tar.gz
+   - Create certifier submission:
+     python3 ops/av/certifier/submission_package.py --out /tmp/certifier_submission.tar.gz --cosign-key $COSIGN_KMS_URI --s3 $S3_UPLOAD
+   - Use ops/av/certifier/submit_to_certifier.sh to sign/upload and send to reviewer with ops/governance/auditor_cover_letter.md
+
+Acceptance checklist (minimum)
+- RT: p99_ok true and safe_ok true for all representative ECUs/buses.
+- HIL: All critical scenarios pass; waveform compare MSE < threshold.
+- Perception: FN rate in critical envelope <= target (set in detailed_test_matrix.csv).
+- Supply chain: All images in manifests cosign-signed and Rekor provenance present.
+- Carbon: Enforce mode tuned; override process documented and tested.
+- Evidence: Signed bundles exist in S3 and evidence manifests recorded.
+
+If any step fails, escalate to Controls Lead / Safety Officer with bundle path and failing artifacts.
+
